            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for a homemaker, then the Persian for a capable housewife."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: جمع کردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جمع کردن (jam' kardan) — \"to tidy up; to gather\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بچه ها اتاقشان را جمع کردند. bachchehâ otâqashân râ jam' kardand. The children tidied their room."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "jam' 'gathering' + kardan. Also 'to collect' and, in sums, 'to add'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "jam' was borrowed from Arabic jamʿ, 'gathering' (EtymDB). kardan, 'to do', is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
